# JARVIS secrets (R16): copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# .env is git-ignored and must never be committed.

# F2's Q&A/small-talk piece (jarvis/speech/qa.py): Groq's free-tier API.
# Get a free key at https://console.groq.com/keys -- no credit card
# needed. Everything else in F2 (wake word, speech-to-text) stays fully
# local/offline and needs no key. If this is missing, that one feature
# degrades to a spoken message saying exactly what to set up and where
# (settings.toml [setup_messages] groq_no_key: "Searching online isn't set
# up yet. Add GROQ_API_KEY to the .env file in the JARVIS folder, then try
# again."); never a crash, and everything else keeps working (decision C,
# R14). Weather (Open-Meteo) needs no key.
GROQ_API_KEY=
